Expose Dawn's Vulkan device, physical device, queue and queue family.

OpenXR requires an application to submit its eye images on the SAME Vulkan
device the compositor was told about at session creation. Aurora owns that
device through Dawn, so the OpenXR backend cannot create its own: it has to
borrow Dawn's.

Dawn's public VulkanBackend.h exposes only VkInstance, which is not enough to
fill XrGraphicsBindingVulkan2KHR. Every handle needed is already reachable
internally (Device::GetVkDevice / GetGraphicsQueueFamily,
PhysicalDevice::GetVkPhysicalDevice, Queue::GetVkQueue), and GetVkDevice is in
fact already defined in VulkanBackend.cpp but never declared in the header.
This publishes them, mirroring the D3D12 backend, which already exports both
its device and its command queue through GetD3D12Device and
GetD3D12CommandQueue.

Additive and upstream-shaped: no existing declaration or behaviour changes.
Applied to the vendored Dawn tree by aurora-main/cmake/AuroraDawnProvider.cmake
when AURORA_DAWN_PROVIDER=vendor, which is the only configuration the
standalone Quest target uses.

diff --git a/include/dawn/native/VulkanBackend.h b/include/dawn/native/VulkanBackend.h
index 355c4b864..a7816b8f8 100644
--- a/include/dawn/native/VulkanBackend.h
+++ b/include/dawn/native/VulkanBackend.h
@@ -39,6 +39,21 @@ namespace dawn::native::vulkan {
 
 DAWN_NATIVE_EXPORT VkInstance GetInstance(WGPUDevice device);
 
+// The remaining handles that describe Dawn's Vulkan device to another API.
+// These mirror d3d12::GetD3D12Device/GetD3D12CommandQueue and exist for the
+// same reason: an interop client (here OpenXR) must use Dawn's own device and
+// queue rather than creating a second one.
+DAWN_NATIVE_EXPORT VkPhysicalDevice GetVkPhysicalDevice(WGPUDevice device);
+
+DAWN_NATIVE_EXPORT VkDevice GetVkDevice(WGPUDevice device);
+
+// The queue backing the device's default WGPUQueue.
+DAWN_NATIVE_EXPORT VkQueue GetVkQueue(WGPUDevice device);
+
+// The queue family GetVkQueue belongs to. Needed to create command pools whose
+// buffers can be submitted onto that queue.
+DAWN_NATIVE_EXPORT uint32_t GetGraphicsQueueFamily(WGPUDevice device);
+
 DAWN_NATIVE_EXPORT PFN_vkVoidFunction GetInstanceProcAddr(WGPUDevice device, const char* pName);
 
 enum class NeedsDedicatedAllocation {
